## Commands (always use these, never ad-hoc tool invocations)

- `make setup` — check that the tools this repo needs are present (nothing is installed) <!-- kept: none -->
- `make lint` — check the marketplace and plugin manifests (`tools/plugin_lint.py`) <!-- kept: none -->
- `make test` — run the tests (`tests/run.sh`) <!-- kept: none -->
- `make check` — everything CI runs offline. **Run it before you say a task is done.** <!-- kept: word -->
- `make validate` — the official Claude Code validator (needs network; CI runs it) <!-- kept: none -->
- `make bump V=patch|minor|major` — set the next version in every manifest and the changelog <!-- kept: none -->

## Before you change a plugin

1. Read `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` to see which plugins exist and where they live. <!-- kept: none -->
2. Read the plugin's own `README.md` and the skill, command or hook you are about to change. <!-- kept: none -->
3. Try the result from this checkout: `claude --plugin-dir plugins/<name>`. <!-- kept: none -->

## Rules

- One folder per plugin under `plugins/<name>/`, each with `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`. <!-- kept: word -->
- A plugin's `source` in the marketplace is never the repository root: an install copies the whole
  source folder. <!-- kept: plugin-lint -->
- A skill is `skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, and `name` in its front matter equals the folder name. <!-- kept: word -->
- Keep every `description` short (at most 1024 characters): it says what the plugin or skill is for
  and when to use it. Release notes go in `CHANGELOG.md`, never in a description. <!-- kept: word -->
- Never edit a version by hand. `make bump` changes every manifest together. <!-- kept: plugin-lint -->
- Scripts and hooks run on other people's machines: standard library only, no network call and no
  write outside the project unless the skill says so and the user can see it. <!-- kept: word -->
- Every behaviour change comes with a test and a line under "Unreleased" in `CHANGELOG.md`. <!-- kept: word -->
- Never commit secrets. <!-- kept: secret-scan -->
- Never commit `.env`. <!-- kept: word -->
- Keep changes small and focused; one concern per PR. <!-- kept: word -->
- Commit messages follow Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `chore:`). <!-- kept: commit-format -->

## After you finish a task

- `make check` is green. <!-- kept: word -->
- `CHANGELOG.md` has a line for the change, written for the people who install the plugin. <!-- kept: word -->
- A significant choice (a new plugin, a changed contract between plugins, a dropped feature) gets a
  short record in `docs/decisions/NNNN-title.md`: context, decision, consequences. <!-- kept: word -->

## Project map

- `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` — the list of plugins this repository offers <!-- kept: none -->
- `plugins/<name>/` — one plugin: manifest, skills, and its own README <!-- kept: none -->
- `tests/` — offline tests <!-- kept: none -->
- `tools/` — manifest lint and version bump (run through `make`) <!-- kept: none -->
- `docs/decisions/` — decision records, when there are any <!-- kept: none -->
- `.claude/skills/` — procedures for agents working on this repository (independent review) <!-- kept: none -->
